# Change Log

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## [3.1.0] - 20/07/2026
- Introduced new optional application: cspy-disord (requires Orgdisord)
    - A workflow for generating and analysing disordered and mixed crystals 
    - cspy-disord prepare-cif prepares the input file for enumeration
    - cspy-disord enumerate enumerates configurations via Orgdisord to produce a .db
    - cspy-disord optimise optimises the structures in the enumerated .db via cspy-opt
    - cspy-disord calc calculate ensemble free energies from the optimised database.
- Databases
    - Introduced new cspy-db function: cspy-db build
        - Allows for the conversion of res files to CSPy database files
    - Overhauled cspy-db dump for more flexible functionality:
        - Files can now be dumped by id.
        - Files can now be dumped within an arbitrary energy-density window 
        - Files can now be dumped from a specific space group
    - Added functionality to perform COMPACK comparisons between databases
- Thresholding
    - New cspy-threshold-utils subcommand: 'intra'. 
        - Allows finding the indices of the atoms in molecules that satisfy SMILES or SMART strings. Useful to setup  intramolecular moves in MC jobs.
- Reoptimise
    - cspy-reoptimise will now report to a status.txt file
- SAUCE
    - Changes to cspy-sauce extract_uc2au
        - Extracted asymmetric units can now be added to existing databases
        - Fixed bugs related to extracting asymmetric units
    - When running SAUCE, the asymmetric unit database can now be specified in the cspy.toml file
        - When using this functionality, SAUCE will use exactly as many AUs as are in the db. (No further are generated.)
- Bug fixes
    - Fixed bug related to restarting reoptimisations
        - When restarting from a database with a '.' it would run all the optimisations again. This is now been fixed.
    - Fixed bug with cspy-setup command missing from pyproject.toml
    - Fixed rounding error in GPlus
    - Fixed bugs in capy-templating app
    - Changed capitalisation when edditing settings of ccdc MaximumCommonSubstructure function
    - Added missing return statements to end analogue generation on failure
    - Fix an issue of the chirality of molecules changing when aligning the molecule.
    - Fix an issue of the CIF parser that would sometimes read the atomic positions from the file as strings and not floats.
    - Removed potentials from available potentials list in cases where potential files are unavailable
    - Fixed bug that would cause cores to get stuck when NEIGHCRYS threw an error
        - This could lead to situations where jobs would stay at 999/1000 crystals until the job timed out

