## [3.0.0] - 13/05/2026
- Rebased mol-CSPy to restablish git trace with developer's internal branch
- Introduced CspyApp and AppHeader classes
    - Major apps, when run, will now print a header with relevant information
    - Centralised code used for setting up mol-CSPy apps
- Introduced ASE interface
    - ASE may now will be used for geometry optimisations / singlepoints
    - We support several simple calculators by default
        - TIP3P
        - TIP4P
        - Lennard-Jones
        - Morse
        - dev-calculator (not for production use)
        - n2p2 (example model bundled with cspy)
        - MACE (models must be provided)
    - We also support custom user-created calculators
        - Calculator needs only be dropped into cspy/ase/calculators
        - See dev-calculator.py or n2p2.py as examples
- Flex
    - Implemented method for CSP on molecules with flexibility
    - conf app introduced to sample conformers from optimised molecule
    - mol_dis app introduced to distort molecules around conformational minima
    - cspy_flex app introduced for running cspy where distorted conformers are sampled from a database
    - See paper for full details
- Thresholding
    - Running threshold jobs still uses the same commands as previously
    - To make life easier a `cspy-threshold-utils` app has been added
        - Can be used to create the disconnectivity graphs
        - Can merge multiple threshold databases into a single one
        - Can be used to setup the initial crystal structures, ensuring they have the right number of molecules
- Introduced Sensible Asymmetric Units for Crystal Exploration (SAUCE)
    - A method for efficient multicomponent CSP
    - Apps/sauce.py offers several sauce related functions
    - In its simplest use case, SAUCE can be enabled as a flag in cspy-csp
    - See paper for full details
- Introduced gplus app
    - Used to efficiently generate multicomponent CSP when the same molecule/ions is used in different systems
    - gplus stores single molecule/ion input files into a database, and can then combine those input files for a multicomponent system
- Added Templating
    - A method for producing unoptimised crystal structures of a target molecule, that are analogous to a given set of template crystal structures
    - Functions in templating/analog_production.py and templating/analog_production_ccdc.py offer related functions
    - Output of replace_molecules_by_substructure method of crystal.py edited to return new asymmetric unit molecules, and the RMSDS of the overlays
- New cspy-db utility
    - cspy-db info can be used to summarise the content of a cspy database
    - cspy-db plot can be used to plot the landscape of a cspy database
- Updated default parameters
    - cspy_defaults.toml file is now blank
    - mol-CSPy will no longer try to read parameters from hidden .cspy.toml file
    - default dmacrys and pmin timings changed to 1200 seconds
    - default basis set for multiploe recalculation following DFTB+ in relevant multi step cspy_reopt calculations is now 6-311G** 

